    "result_text": "The build is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity. Every change flows from one rule: the **`V2` version tag is mixed into the identifiers only**, while user-facing region fields stay the plain region code.\n\n**Identity derivation (region code inside the identifiers \u2192 V2)**\n- `Localities.java` \u2014 added `IDENTITY_VERSION = \"V2\"`, `identityRegion(postcode)` (returns e.g. `V2NSW`), and `timezoneOfPostcode(...)`. Because every V1 region is a bare letter run (`NSW`, `VIC`, `QLD`, `UNKNOWN`) and V2 begins `V2\u2026`, no V1 identifier is reproduced.\n- `AssignOwnerMemberId` \u2014 the `REGION` segment now uses `identityRegion(...)`, so `memberId` becomes `V2NSW263F9A0C714`.\n- `OwnerHousehold` \u2014 `householdId` hashes `<V2>|<normalizedLastName>|<postcode>`.\n- `OwnerIdentityKey` \u2014 `identityKey` hashes `<V2>|<telephone>|<email>|<soundex(lastName)>`. The tag is a constant added to all owners, so duplicate-equality semantics are unchanged.\n\n**Response shape**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an `OwnerIdentity` schema, added top-level integer `apiVersion`, replaced the three top-level identifier fields with `identity: $ref OwnerIdentity`.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 maps `apiVersion = 2` and builds the nested `identity` object; **kept `locality`/`timezone` plain** by deriving them from the postcode region (not from the now-V2 memberId).\n\n**Owner segment** \u2014 `ownerSegment` recomputed from the plain postcode region, so `METRO`/`REGIONAL` detection still works under the V2 memberId (the `V2` tag never enters the segment's region).\n\n**Audit schema \u2192 v2** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` gained `schemaVersion = 2` (in the record and JSON); the `memberId` it carries is the V2 identifier. Verified in the log: `{\"seq\":1,...,\"memberId\":\"V2NSW2716E6609E7\",...,\"schemaVersion\":2}`.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged throughout.",
