    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands. The endpoint is a 22-step OfficeFloor pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`); every step from `normalizeAddress` onward runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is rejected before the pipeline runs.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *(validation / short-circuit)* Reads only the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key already maps to an owner in `IdempotencyStore`, throws `IdempotentReplayException` (returns the original owner, ~200) instead of creating a duplicate. No key or unseen key \u2192 continues.\n\n**2. `NormalizeOwnerAddress`** \u2014 *(side-effect; the one `@RequestBody` bind)* Reads the body once and republishes it. Prefers structured form (`addressLine1`/`addressLine2`) when `addressLine1` is non-blank, else the flat `address`. Normalizes each supplied line (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations) and sets flat `address` to the composed normalized value.\n\n**3. `RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 *(validation)* Rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` if any of `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` is null/blank (listing all offenders). Runs after normalization, so an address blank-after-normalization counts as missing.\n\n**4. `ValidateOwnerPostcode`** \u2014 *(validation)* Postcode optional. When present it must be exactly 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099 via `Localities`) the code must fall in that inclusive range. Otherwise `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n**5. `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 *(validation)* `registrationDate` optional. If supplied and after `LocalDate.now()`, rejects with `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`** \u2014 *(side-effect + validation)* Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps country code after a leading `+`, else assumes `+61` (dropping one leading `0`). Result must be 8\u201315 digits; national length must match country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Writes E.164 value back in place; invalid \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n**7. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`** \u2014 *(side-effect + validation)* Email optional. When present, lower-cases in place and requires syntactic validity; invalid \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (400).\n\n**8. `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 *(validation)* If email present and its domain is blocklisted (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), rejects with `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n**9. `CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity`** \u2014 *(validation)* The sole hard-duplicate check. Computes `OwnerIdentityKey` = SHA-256 of `telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`; if it equals any non-soft-deleted existing owner's key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n**10. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 *(validation)* If the request's city already holds \u2265 `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` owners (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed), rejects with `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**11. `CheckDailyOwnerLimit`** \u2014 *(validation)* Rolls `LocalDate.now()` forward past weekends (`BusinessDay`); if \u2265 100 (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) owners already have that registration date, rejects with `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n**12. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Maps the validated/normalized DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`. (No owner exists before this point, so every rejection above avoids creating one.)\n\n**13. `AssignOwnerHousehold`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n\n**14. `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Effective date = supplied date or `LocalDate.now()`; rolls a weekend forward to Monday (`BusinessDay`); writes it onto the owner.\n\n**15. `AssignOwnerMemberId`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Sets `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (V2 region from postcode, 2-digit fiscal year of the adjusted date, 8 upper-hex SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName`, Luhn check digit); appends `-<n>` (n\u22652) to break collisions with existing owners.\n\n**16. `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Sets `namesakeCount` = count of already-stored owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n**17. `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Defaults `possibleDuplicate=false`/`possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Unless `sharesHousehold` is true or postcode is null, scans non-deleted owners: a different identity key but same last-name soundex and same postcode \u2192 sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=that owner's id`.\n\n**18. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n**19. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Records the `Idempotency-Key` \u2192 new owner id in `IdempotencyStore` (no-op if no key). Enables step 1's replay.\n\n**20. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Logs a human-readable line plus an immutable `OwnerCreatedEvent` (sequence number, id, memberId as primary identifier, membershipLevel) to the `AUDIT` logger.\n\n**21. `EnqueueWelcomeNotification`** \u2014 *(side-effect)* Emits a welcome line (owner id + memberId) to the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n**22. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 *(side-effect / response)* Maps to `OwnerDto`, computes and attaches `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning` and `riskFlag`, and returns `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n- **Validations that can reject (in order):** authorization \u2192 idempotency replay \u2192 required fields \u2192 postcode \u2192 registration date \u2192 telephone format \u2192 email format \u2192 disposable email \u2192 duplicate identity (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429).\n- **Ordering intent:** all rejecting checks precede `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner`, so no owner is persisted on any failure; normalization steps precede the checks that depend on the normalized values (e.g. required-field check sees the composed address; identity/telephone checks use the E.164 number)."
